DDEESSCCRRIIPPTTIIOONN
       Don’t use this function.  Use ssiiggssuussppeenndd(2) instead.

       The  function  ssiiggppaauussee()  is  designed  to  wait  for some signal.  It
       changes the process’s signal mask (set of blocked  signals),  and  then
       waits  for  a signal to arrive.  Upon arrival of a signal, the original
       signal mask is restored.

